   "evidence": "HEAD client-port.ts:13 requires `/^\\d+$/.test(explicit)`, rejecting +49751, decimal and exponent spellings that HEAD config.ts:287 accepts through `num(Number(process.env.LIMITLESS_PORT) || server.port, 7400)`. api-token.ts:33\u201336 authorizes the incorrectly resolved port; lines 43 and 49 invoke that fallback for missing and stale bindings. A separate temporary probe intercepted fetch calls without network access: the CLI, default lease client and httpBackend each prepared requests to port 49752 carrying the synthetic bearer, for both missing and stale bindings. Base had the same daemon rule but no client-port resolver; its lease client used `Number(process.env.LIMITLESS_PORT ?? 7400)`, which correctly selected 49751. Base's unrestricted token disclosure was already defective, but this change introduces the divergent resolver and routing."
