   "evidence": "At head, src/cli/client-port.ts:11-13 accepts the environment port only if it matches `/^\\d+$/`, so `+49751` falls through to the configured `[server] port`. The daemon at src/config.ts:287 uses `num(Number(process.env.LIMITLESS_PORT) || server.port, 7400)`, which reads `+49751` as 49751. The fallback in src/cli/api-token.ts:32-36 attaches the bearer token to `http://127.0.0.1:${resolveClientPort()}`, which is a port the daemon is not listening on. Configured port 0 also differs: the daemon gets 0 (an ephemeral port), but `isClientPort(0)` is false, so the client uses 7400."
